article en "Sentence"
body
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence cons code "syntax.neplg" cons text " defines the independent structured-sentence surface, with root " cons code "Sentence" cons text " and category " cons code "Inline" cons text ". " nil
    cons "The production Grammar compiler builds its LanguagePackage; the development host registers the Name and Sentence literal reader operations explicitly. "
    cons "Neither Doc nor Math is a required schema."
    nil
  cons rawcode some "text" "sentence\n  cons ruby text \"漢\" text \"かん\"\n  cons anno text \"語\" cons text \"note\" nil\n  nil\n"
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence cons text "The corresponding literal is " cons code "\"[漢/かん]{語/note}\"" cons text ". " nil
    cons "Literal token structure and the prefix parse tree remain distinct. "
    cons "The semantic equivalence of the two is part of the lower/check/print acceptance, not proven by parsing alone."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "The surface accepts whitespace separation. "
    cons sentence cons text "It does not skip " cons code "#" cons text " comments. " nil
    cons "Annotation belongs to the separate target-wrapper contract; document structure belongs to Doc. "
    cons sentence cons text "See " cons link relative "../../doc/spec/23-sentence-annotation.md" none text "spec 23" cons text "." nil
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "LanguagePackage compilation and native/owned prefix parsing are implemented. "
    cons "The standard prefix printer emits all ten forms, keeping constructor boundaries and escaping BuiltinText. "
    cons "Foreign-inline output needs its selected surface adapter. "
    cons "Standard prefix lowering returns a checked meaning arena and a mapping back to the retained syntax bundle. "
    cons "The presentation entry handles literal payloads and prefix forms with their source locations and views. "
    cons "Foreign adapters and Doc body migration remain in progress; this is not a completed document migration."
    nil
  nil
